INT. ELIAB'S HOUSE - DUSK #4#

Supper. One lamp on the low olive-wood table, its smoke turning in the last grey light of the open door. Beyond it the gate lamp, lit again, small in the dusk, moths already moving around it. The whole household eats: hired men at the far end, Miriam at the hearth, the dog under the table. Through the door, dogs bark on the other farms down the valley.

Eliab breaks the bread.

ELIAB
Blessed are you, O LORD our God, King of the world, who brings forth bread from the earth.

MICAH
Sixty measures, master. The tithe is set apart, and the fifth for the store.

ASHER
This house has never seen a bad year.

ELIAB
Because we kept the store in every good one.

ASHER
Count the ewe twice, Micah. She came home on a better beast than the rest.

Eliab laughs out loud. The hired men laugh. Amos eats in silence.

ASHER
Father. Sixty measures, the flock, the vines. What is all of it worth?

AMOS
(low)
Eat, Asher.

ELIAB
Worth? One day it shall be yours and your brother's.

Asher has not broken his bread. He looks at Amos, who chews with his eyes on the table. He looks through the door at the gate lamp. Then he sets the bread down flat on the table, and keeps his hand on it.

FLASH. A dog trotting off across a field with a round of bread in its jaws.

ASHER
Father, give me the portion of your goods that falls to me.

Silence. The hired men stop chewing. Miriam's hand stops on the pot.

Amos sets his bread down, his jaw tight, his eyes on his father.

Eliab looks at Amos first. Amos won't meet his eyes.

Eliab looks down at the bread in his hands, and for a long moment he does not move.

ELIAB
You know what you ask.

Asher holds his father's eyes.

ELIAB
Your portion will be silver, son, and silver runs faster than any man who carries it.

ELIAB
Every morning you chose your bed, and I let you choose it.

Asher looks down.

ELIAB
Now you choose the road.

Nobody at the table moves.

ELIAB
Tomorrow I divide my living. To your brother his part, and to you yours.

AMOS
(quietly)
Write mine if you must, Father. Then keep it. I am going nowhere.

